OL,3,ABurnham says he wants to cut welfare
OL,4,Abill 'as soon as we possibly can'
OL,5,
OL,6,FAndy Burnham has said he wants to cut
OL,7,Fthe welfare bill "as soon as we
OL,8,Fpossibly can", but was unable to
OL,9,Fguarantee this would happen before the
OL,10,Fnext general election.
OL,12,FOpponents raised concerns over the lack
OL,13,Fof details on welfare reform in
OL,14,FWednesday's Budget, after welfare
OL,15,Fspending was forecast to increase from
OL,16,F#353bn this year to #431bn in 2031/32.
OL,23,APub: 29-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG3/39
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
FL,303,300,200,140,0,100
PN,11904
SC,0004
CT,25,T
PS,c000
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F119A1793296565
OL,1,W5j 5Q7kjs15j 5ws
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q%**,$-.,%,. (,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,ABurnham says he wants to cut welfare
OL,4,Abill 'as soon as we possibly can'
OL,5,
OL,6,FAsked whether he would seek to reduce
OL,7,Fthe bill before the next election,
OL,8,FBurnham told reporters: "We want to get
OL,9,Fthe welfare bill down as quickly as
OL,10,Fpossible, and we're working flat out to
OL,11,Fthat end."
OL,13,FHe warned against "crude cuts" and said
OL,14,Fhe wants to get people into
OL,15,F"sustainable employment". The
OL,16,FConservatives accused Labour of being
OL,17,F"addicted to welfare".
OL,23,APub: 29-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG4/39
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
